#
# prima-materia — the searches of the protocol on the clause that puts the
# effect beyond the bystander
#
# Two corpora were put the same question: does the transmission show an
# operation of public effect to people who are not the operator, or does it
# withdraw it from them, and where does it say which. The protocol itself is
# at examinations/the-effect-put-beyond-the-bystander-tested.ttl.
#

pmp:BystanderVisuddhimaggaSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the handbook that reserves the changed ground to the operator also shows its operations to others"@en, "Ob das Handbuch, das den verwandelten Boden dem Vollzieher vorbehält, seine Verrichtungen auch anderen zeigt"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Buddhaghosa, Visuddhimagga XII.69-101, in Pe Maung Tin, The Path of Purity, Part II (PTS Translation Series 17), pp. 452-460, in Ñāṇamoli, The Path of Purification (BPS edition 2011), and in the Pali of the Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana edition, Visuddhimagga II, paragraphs 388-391; with Saṃyutta Nikāya 41.4, which the handbook quotes, in the Pali of the same edition and in Woodward, The Book of the Kindred Sayings IV (PTS 1927), pp. 197-199" ;
    pm:searchedFor "Whether the chapter that carries pmc:TassaYevaSaPathavi states or narrates any operation of public effect performed so that people other than the operator see it, and whether it says anything about when the operator's wish to extend the perception is exercised." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The passages were read continuously in the two English translations from the miracle of appearing to the travel through the air, and the Pali was located by Saṅkassa, pākaṭapāṭihāriya, tirobhāva and adhiṭṭhāsi and read over the same span. In the discourse the Pali was located by Mahakapāṭihāriya and read to its end, and Woodward's English by Mahaka and Macchikasanda." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundOpposing ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:PakataPatihariya, pmc:MahakaPatihariya ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-18" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-18" ;
    skos:note "The handbook names a class of miracle by its being seen together with its performer and gives five cases of it, every one before an assembly or a city; the earlier reading of the same paragraphs had entered the capacity and left the cases. The discourse it quotes for the opposite class gives two effects a layman saw, one of them on his request for a proof, and ends with the performer leaving the place for good."@en ;
    skos:note "The limit of the search. The commentary and subcommentary on the passage, which would say how the order read these cases against its rule against display, were not opened."@en .

pmp:BystanderChukcheeSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the Chukchee practice performs its feats before strangers, and under what conditions"@en, "Ob die tschuktschische Praxis ihre Kunststücke vor Fremden ausführt, und unter welchen Bedingungen"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Waldemar Bogoras, The Chukchee, Memoir of the American Museum of Natural History vol. VII (Leiden: E. J. Brill, 1904-1909), pp. 415-423 and 435-447, and p. 301" ;
    pm:searchedFor "Whether the corpus reports feats with an effect a bystander would see performed before people who are not the practitioner, whether any is offered as a proof to a doubter, and whether the corpus states a condition that withholds such an effect from a stranger's sight or check. The question was put here because the falsifier of pmc:TheEffectPutBeyondTheBystander names the Siberian material as the first place to look." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The English text was read continuously over the pages named; the section headings Ventriloquism and Other Tricks and Tricks performed in the Light located the second stretch. The text layer was checked for its share of Latin letters before reading, 0.997, and its running heads for sequence. The whole volume was also searched for ventriloquism, stab, knife, in the light, trick, belly, convince and sceptic, which located the passage on the spirits coming only in the darkness at p. 301; the other hits outside the stretch read were not followed." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundOpposing ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:ChukcheeShamanShunsStrangers, pmc:ChukcheePowerCannotBeHidden, pmc:ChukcheeManifestationsInTheDark, pmc:ChukcheeSpiritsNotToBeTouched, pmc:ChukcheeNoSeparateVoicesByDaylight, pmc:ChukcheeContestOfPractitioners, pmc:ChukcheeSelfStabbing, pmc:ChukcheeProofForbiddenByASpirit, pmc:ChukcheeBirthDestroysInspiration, pmc:ChukcheeBrightEyesSeeSpirits, pmc:ChukcheeHardToKill, pmc:ChukcheeRefusedCallKills, pmc:ChukcheeWolfTransformation, pmc:ChukcheeDrumMendedSign, pmc:ChukcheePredictionOfTheParting ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-18" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-18" ;
    skos:note "Both halves of the statement's question are answered in the same corpus. The séance is held in the dark, its spirits may not be touched, and the voices are not produced in daylight; feats on the body are performed in the light and even by day, and at a ceremonial every practitioner present must show his ability and is paid by it. One feat was offered as a proof to the recorder and withdrawn at the last moment by a voice of the performance."@en ;
    skos:note "The limit of the search. One recorder, in English; the separate volume of Chukchee Materials, which carries the texts in the language and to which several of the cases are referred, was not opened, and the chapter was read in two stretches and not whole."@en .
